      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T13:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rereviewing this, I just realized that the latest iteration does the following for `getBinding\u003cT\u003e(binding, i)`:\n\n```\nif (i \u003c metadata.arrayLength \u0026\u0026 TypeIdOf\u003cT\u003e \u003d\u003d metadata.bindings[i]) {\n    return bindings[i];\n} else {\n    return bindings[metadata.arrayLengthWithDefaultBindings - i];\n}\n```\n\nWhich needs a second array length in the metadata. Instead we should do:\n\n```\nif (i \u003c metadata.arrayLength \u0026\u0026 TypeIdOf\u003cT\u003e \u003d\u003d metadata.bindings[i]) {\n    return bindings[i];\n} else {\n    return bindings[metadata.arrayLength + i];\n}\n```\n\nTo have a single arrayLength in the metadata. This means that we no longer need the constraint on `kTextureNull`!\n\nCan we have the pseudo code above in this class, so that it serves as documentation of where Dawn needs to add the default bindings?",
      "revId": "30cc213d6672c535801eedd53011c38688d5c143",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cfcc091_f4bf459f",
