      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T14:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would type-full be sparse? There is only one type, so we don\u0027t really need to do anything other then swap in array length. Any out of bounds access will just return an item in the array (similar to what we do now)",
      "parentUuid": "0fa04a85_3d9c5c1d",
      "revId": "30cc213d6672c535801eedd53011c38688d5c143",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aea47ffc_5608a099",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/transform/runtime_binding_array.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
